WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.770
Today, I want to talk about energy.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:06.620
Energy is the key, the source of
your success in language learning

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.000
and in so many things in life.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.080
And I want to talk about six tips on
how to generate energy within yourself

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.730
and how to maintain that energy.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.889
I think I'm allowed to talk about
that because I'm 78 and so I've

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.760
lived a lot longer than most of
the people watching this video.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.430
And so I have a lot of life experience.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.669
The first thing about energy
is the more active you are,

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.350
the more energy you create.

00:00:29.565 --> 00:00:34.185
So while I talk about input in language
learning and the need to bring the

00:00:34.185 --> 00:00:37.535
language into you, because you don't
have the language inside you, when it

00:00:37.535 --> 00:00:41.235
comes to that energy, which is driving
you to learn a language or to do anything

00:00:41.235 --> 00:00:43.565
else, you create that within yourself.

00:00:43.765 --> 00:00:47.055
Now, it may be true that some
people are born with more natural

00:00:47.075 --> 00:00:50.444
energy, that it's a part of their
makeup more than other people.

00:00:50.454 --> 00:00:54.964
However, whatever your sort of
starting point is, your, uh, inherent.

00:00:55.375 --> 00:00:59.555
Energy level, you can
improve it by being active.

00:00:59.675 --> 00:01:04.064
And so even in terms of business, if
you don't give, if you don't volunteer,

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:08.324
if you don't offer to do things, if you
wait until you get the reward before

00:01:08.325 --> 00:01:10.244
you do things, you won't be successful.

00:01:10.365 --> 00:01:13.664
You've got to be proactive and
you've got to give before you get.

00:01:13.884 --> 00:01:17.975
And if you're active and want to
generate that energy level, you

00:01:17.975 --> 00:01:19.785
will be rewarded with more energy.

00:01:19.975 --> 00:01:22.565
You're not going to lose
energy by being active.

00:01:22.604 --> 00:01:25.054
You have to generate the
energy by being active.

00:01:25.054 --> 00:01:27.094
It's like your internal dynamo.

00:01:27.344 --> 00:01:28.335
So that's point number one.

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:32.384
Second point, you want to be active
both physically and mentally.

00:01:32.535 --> 00:01:33.634
The two are related.

00:01:33.904 --> 00:01:37.464
So when it comes to language learning,
if you are active physically,

00:01:37.475 --> 00:01:38.894
you're going to be more successful.

00:01:39.225 --> 00:01:42.125
In your mental activity
of learning a language.

00:01:42.385 --> 00:01:46.175
So that means get in the habit
of doing regular exercises.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.174
Every morning I have my
seven minute routine.

00:01:48.195 --> 00:01:50.095
It's not a lot, but it's balanced.

00:01:50.314 --> 00:01:51.775
I don't know what's coming at me.

00:01:52.005 --> 00:01:56.395
Burpees, pushups, you know, crunches,
whatever it might be, I do them.

00:01:56.825 --> 00:01:58.355
And there's a double benefit.

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:02.225
A, the benefit that I'm that little
bit fitter for having done that,

00:02:02.485 --> 00:02:05.735
but also the sense of satisfaction
that comes from having done it.

00:02:06.279 --> 00:02:07.809
Carries with me through the day.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:13.980
Remember, very often we don't know what
we are achieving, but if we are active

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.299
and we sort of tick that one off, I did
my morning exercise, you feel energized,

00:02:18.329 --> 00:02:22.260
you feel good for the day, and you
are in fact improving your physical.

00:02:22.495 --> 00:02:23.855
Energy source.

00:02:24.175 --> 00:02:28.155
Now, the third point is with physical
activity, like working out and language

00:02:28.155 --> 00:02:30.195
learning, it's the activity that counts.

00:02:30.225 --> 00:02:33.115
If you're running a race, if
you're jogging, you don't need

00:02:33.115 --> 00:02:34.495
to be looking over your shoulder.

00:02:34.635 --> 00:02:36.095
It's the fact that you're doing it.

00:02:36.144 --> 00:02:37.424
That's going to make you feel good.

00:02:37.635 --> 00:02:40.674
That's going to give you a
sense of achievement, whether

00:02:40.675 --> 00:02:42.374
it's dopamine or serotonin.

00:02:42.374 --> 00:02:44.384
I'm not too clear, but
you feel good because.

00:02:44.665 --> 00:02:45.195
You did it.

00:02:45.245 --> 00:02:47.035
So it's the activity that matters.

00:02:47.185 --> 00:02:48.645
And it's the same in language learning.

00:02:48.785 --> 00:02:51.925
That's why at LingQ, we don't
try to measure what you have

00:02:51.925 --> 00:02:53.855
achieved, how much you improved.

00:02:54.035 --> 00:02:59.475
If I spend an hour on LingQ, on my
iPad, looking up words and reading

00:02:59.475 --> 00:03:00.885
and listening or whatever I do.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:04.880
What matters to me is that I did
that activity and I get a sense

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.720
of satisfaction, achievement.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:07.700
I accomplished something.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.009
I put that amount of effort
into my language learning.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.040
That's what matters.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:15.230
The amount that I improved during that
session, it's hard for me to measure.

00:03:15.519 --> 00:03:18.889
So give yourself credit
for actually being active.

00:03:19.169 --> 00:03:20.259
You'll get a good feeling.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.910
I did something and that generates energy.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:26.570
Now number four, try to
control your impulses.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.170
Try to control your.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:33.090
Ability to resist temptation, if
you are studying, say on your iPad,

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:36.959
develop that ability to resist those
distractions, looking up the email,

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:40.220
looking up Twitter, looking up whatever
other things you follow, don't do it.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:45.039
Every time you do it, your right
prefrontal cortex is getting

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:48.960
stronger at that ability to
resist temptation and distraction.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.340
If you give in to distraction,
you are weakening that ability

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:54.714
in your prefrontal cortex.

00:03:54.965 --> 00:03:55.615
cortex.

00:03:55.625 --> 00:04:00.365
So it's very important to be able to
stick with what you're doing, resist

00:04:00.365 --> 00:04:06.065
the distractions, and by the same token,
resist the temptation to Eat, you know,

00:04:06.265 --> 00:04:11.024
food that you know is not good for you
because good eating, good diet obviously

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:13.325
also contributes to our energy level.

00:04:13.464 --> 00:04:17.074
Resist the temptation to fly off
the handle and get mad at someone.

00:04:17.105 --> 00:04:19.214
That also saps our energy.

00:04:19.234 --> 00:04:25.465
So, developing good habits, helping
your prefrontal cortex get stronger at

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:30.215
resisting these negative temptations
is a good part or an important part of

00:04:30.445 --> 00:04:32.635
being full of energy when you need it.

00:04:33.025 --> 00:04:37.515
Now, a fifth point in order to maintain
your energy level, vary your activities.

00:04:37.905 --> 00:04:41.114
I mentioned my morning routine
because it's an app on my iPhone.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.135
I don't know which
exercises are coming at me.

00:04:43.195 --> 00:04:44.015
It's varied.

00:04:44.064 --> 00:04:46.374
If it's the same every
day, I would get bored.

00:04:46.684 --> 00:04:47.984
It's the same with language learning.

00:04:48.424 --> 00:04:49.534
Vary your activities.

00:04:49.674 --> 00:04:50.895
And I've discussed before.

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:56.059
The importance of not block learning, of
interleaving, of moving from one content

00:04:56.119 --> 00:05:01.279
item to another, mixing in reading a book
with reading on the iPad, uh, mixing in

00:05:01.289 --> 00:05:05.299
the listening and the reading, mixing
in advanced material with easy material.

00:05:06.109 --> 00:05:09.949
Keep it varied and that'll maintain
your interest level and interest

00:05:09.949 --> 00:05:12.260
level equates to energy level.

00:05:12.409 --> 00:05:13.710
So vary your activities.

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:18.040
And you will find that your
energy level will be higher.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.560
And finally, another way of ensuring
you always have the energy you need,

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:24.510
is to enjoy what you are doing.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:29.169
So, for example, in terms of
physical activity, I like to take

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:31.150
the stairs two steps at a time.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.679
It's a way of investing energy.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:39.140
And activity into maintaining my
energy level, but I enjoy doing it.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:43.460
I am conscious of taking those two, the
steps two at a time, going up the stairs.

00:05:43.969 --> 00:05:46.730
Also look around, enjoy
the colors around you.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:51.079
Enjoy the texture of the wood or
the whatever, the dress that you see

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:56.710
on someone, the material, enjoy the
scenery, just try to fully appreciate

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:00.899
all the things that surround us and
by the same token, whatever you have

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:02.890
achieved in the language you're learning.

00:06:03.125 --> 00:06:04.835
Give yourself credit for it.

00:06:04.965 --> 00:06:05.895
Enjoy it.

00:06:06.035 --> 00:06:06.995
Enjoy the language.

00:06:07.075 --> 00:06:08.175
Enjoy the activity.

00:06:08.225 --> 00:06:09.445
Enjoy what you have achieved.

00:06:09.775 --> 00:06:10.755
Stay positive.

00:06:10.775 --> 00:06:11.725
Stay in the moment.

00:06:11.985 --> 00:06:15.245
All of those things will contribute
to a higher energy level.

00:06:16.244 --> 00:06:18.114
With that, I'm going to
leave you with two videos.

00:06:18.504 --> 00:06:21.185
One deals with the mental side.

00:06:21.664 --> 00:06:26.034
Of maintaining your energy level
and not chasing down rabbit holes

00:06:26.034 --> 00:06:29.284
and dwelling on negative thoughts,
which maintains our energy level.

00:06:29.695 --> 00:06:32.784
And the other one relates
more to physical activity.

00:06:32.804 --> 00:06:35.844
And it's one that I did about seven
years ago, and you'll see that

00:06:35.844 --> 00:06:38.585
it's quite relevant to this video.

00:06:38.734 --> 00:06:39.884
So thank you for listening.

00:06:40.164 --> 00:06:40.705
Bye for now.

